      "Language": "pol",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "It is known that gastro-esophageal reflux can trigger bronchospasm among children with asthma and cystic fibrosis as well as in children without chronic respiratory tract disorders. In our practice we have met only once with the case of a child misdiagnosed as having severe asthma in whom surgical treatment of gastro-esophageal reflux disease ended with full withdrawal of respiratory symptoms. On the basis of this case we conclude that the diagnostic procedures should be performed in cases of asthma resistant to typical treatment."},
